n matrix that corresponds to a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation is\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRotating the vector ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation). Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}\\begin{bmatrix}6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $b(t)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3976db94-3fa7-56f2-8187-2b59f24f15ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260389} {:answer/id #uuid "842339b8-98c1-5bc8-b21b-5d8dd9baac4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2x \\\\ 2y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261023} {:answer/id #uuid "99e2d75e-446a-58c1-901c-0518d9c06103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261208} {:answer/id #uuid "9bab6ff5-e16d-536f-82ce-b975c03326e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}y \\\\ -x\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261223} {:answer/id #uuid "fc45036a-3adc-550c-a1f8-db9b4bcb853a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860454