nd{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation).\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n||{r}^{′}(t)||=\\sqrt{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}}=2,\n$$\n\nand since for our curve $x(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ it follows that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262667 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b6a36f0-6141-5706-8753-0bd4e0c80b50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5x \\\\ 5y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259981} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf5625e-a55d-590b-8b7b-ad05ed53c16f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}y \\\\ -x\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260531} {:answer/id #uuid "6c31d42f-3cad-5c99-a1d3-8e0da559fcd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260823} {:answer/id #uuid "972ad6b2-940f-5b91-9b16-0f9708d8664b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261186} {:answer/id #uuid "b9e432e3-0dcd-5754-a57d-a86beb7d39ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-x \\\\ y\\