 \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation).\n\nNow, since \n\n$$\n||{r}^{′}(t)||=\\sqrt{(-\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}}=\\sqrt{5},\n$$\n\nand since for our curve $x(t)=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ and $y(t)=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ it follows that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262670 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d7df425-d571-5cc6-a9f9-7fa772ca09d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260418} {:answer/id #uuid "5f862ba0-cbc5-525b-a3db-3428c339522c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260698} {:answer/id #uuid "8b2741fe-a796-5f20-9695-6d599cd52276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261087} {:answer/id #uuid "970078ef-d4d4-525f-8d57-14ffe7573748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261183} {:answer/id #uuid "ae0e6590-8895-55c9-a0d3-7c73ce7b8ec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} 