x}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation). Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $b(t)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262671 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2198f27d-b991-5691-be59-68e071b839e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260164} {:answer/id #uuid "431e0fff-866d-526d-abf4-0591bc494ff3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260461} {:answer/id #uuid "83a5fa37-84d1-5514-bf8f-8c9cadc6a259" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261018} {:answer/id #uuid "998f27e0-f6a3-5021-a440-8c5d289a4d63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261205} {:answer/id #uuid "f10a9893-0d8e-5c78-a46a-beb6d4ae97c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "998f27e0-f6a3-5021-a440-8c5d289a4d63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id