y ${90}^{∘}$ *counterclockwise* to obtain an outward normal vector.\n\nThe rotation matrix that corresponds to a ${90}^{∘}$ counterclockwise rotation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRotating the vector ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ counterclockwise, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -9\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}9\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation). Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}\\begin{bmatrix}9\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{9\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $a(t)=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275232 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02692810-69c5-51d1-8b75-972adfa093a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272403} {:answer/id #uuid "1c337dbd-c56c-53cc-8680-d3230277df72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272632} {:answer/id #uuid "220fdb4d-991c-5f19-b039-9f36ce2bd775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272689} {:answer/id #uuid "9c9b4fec-609c-5430-9e7e-dd4028a70321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273744} {:answer/id #uuid "db2fc322-2cfa-560e-a0a2-d9894b64eb5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186