ted clockwise, we rotate ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ *counterclockwise* to obtain an outward-pointing normal vector.\n\nThe rotation matrix that corresponds to a ${90}^{∘}$ counterclockwise rotation is\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRotating the vector ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ counterclockwise, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}10\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 10\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation). Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}\\begin{bmatrix}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 10\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $b(t)=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420303 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bf4ba5d-ef9f-5153-ae1c-e4c0c5782ebd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420280} {:answer/id #uuid "20fcf7c1-0e53-5bc4-9774-94258e3e649e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420281} {:answer/id #uuid "6113e78e-3c31-5b91-be16-7271edc5b671" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420286} {:answer/id #uuid "c3fbf14d-6a97-5982-90b0-30f215c18cf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420292} {:answer/id #uuid "f7e65222-2412-514f