begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 14\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation). Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 14\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+14\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $a(t)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445291 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12c2611f-f075-5bef-9b12-8e6d7c6016ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445265} {:answer/id #uuid "21912693-46e5-54c5-885b-ffece0e4f4ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445266} {:answer/id #uuid "322819d7-8ec8-5e47-8eb6-5ed5edaa65a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445268} {:answer/id #uuid "b73f5019-9bf1-59b9-bbe0-c37feaebc1f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445280} {:answer/id #uuid "d0954837-8233-5864-88b9-32dce2d50d2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b73f5019-9bf1-59b9-bbe0-c37feaebc1f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445280} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee2b7e94-139d-52df-a733-a979d04555a4" :answer-field/key "selectio