ise rotation is\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nRotating the vector ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ counterclockwise, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation). Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}\\begin{bmatrix}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}=\\frac{5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $a(t)=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522808 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fc41bcd-3417-5400-a54c-1906072f0eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522090} {:answer/id #uuid "280e7321-16c9-5e68-b059-fc36a133c53a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522111} {:answer/id #uuid "809d9373-5abe-50a9-9050-66157bd65485" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522276} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1ba871-8164-5731-8210-1d7c5fc1f375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522298} {:answer/id #uuid "c69dbee9-0364-537c-b998-1950da1608c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522435}] :answer-field/correct {:a